# Copy this file to .env in this folder and fill it in. .env is git-ignored; never commit a real key.
# The launchers do not read a .env file themselves: load it into your shell first, e.g.
#   set -a && source .env && set +a
# Nothing here is needed to run the tests, the stub regression or the text CLI.

# Your TypeSafe API key, used by the live and recording clients (--client jev, --client record,
# and the server with JEV_CLIENT=jev). Recording the cassette needs it; replaying one does not.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# Where the decision model is reached: JEV_PROVIDER, default typesafe. Each provider reads its own key.
#   typesafe     TYPESAFE_API_KEY      https://api.typesafe.ai                 model jev-1.13.0
#   openrouter   OPENROUTER_API_KEY    https://openrouter.ai/api               model typesafe/jev-1.13
#   vercel       AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY    https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/typesafe   model typesafe-ai/jev
#   custom       JEV_API_KEY (optional), JEV_BASE_URL and JEV_MODEL (required): a compatible endpoint,
#                such as an open-weight model that speaks Jev's API. Its probabilities are not Jev's,
#                so the confidence thresholds may need re-measuring: record a cassette with it and
#                compare with regress.
# JEV_BASE_URL and JEV_MODEL also override an official provider's. A base URL must be https unless
# it is localhost. Each model records and replays its own cassette, named after the model.
# JEV_PROVIDER=typesafe
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# JEV_BASE_URL=
# JEV_MODEL=
# JEV_API_KEY=

# The phone line (pnpm serve) needs these three. A 555 number is fine for local use.
# PUBLIC_HOST=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# HANDOFF_NUMBER=
